title: "Sayan Universal Gradient Theory"
authors:
  - name: Sayan M.
version: "2.1.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22723745
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sayan9168/Sayan-Universal-Gradient-Theory"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22723745"
abstract: >-
  Sayan Universal Gradient Theory (SUG) is a proposed mathematical framework
  and Python implementation for a dimensionless scalar field coupling source
  energy, a thermal gradient, and distance. The framework is speculative and
  has not been empirically validated; its numerical outputs are model
  calculations, not established physical measurements.
keywords:
  - computational physics
  - mathematical modeling
  - thermal gradients
  - theoretical physics
